import json,pathlib,statistics,re
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;d=json.loads((p/'results.json').read_text())
lines=['# Compact versus direct16 helper-only comparison','','Measured source `2c14fd9b`, runtime `62fc59f3`. Same-source binaries use explicit direct16 helper-only versus compact helper-only configuration. Neither uses optimized native direct code. Explicit 2 MiB Eden and two 8 MiB old semispaces. All 12 audits and 36 timing processes passed exact artifact hashes, checksums, expected object allocations and real collection checks. Audits use 128 warmups; timings use 100 warmups, nine batches of 32 calls and three rotating process rounds.','','| Case | Backend | Median ms | Process medians ms | Timed minor/full | Go heap MiB | Peak RSS MiB |','|---|---|---:|---|---|---:|---:|']
for c in dict.fromkeys(r['case'] for r in d['rows']):
 for v in ['direct16','compact']:
  rs=[r['result'] for r in d['rows'] if r['case']==c and r['variant']==v];ts=[statistics.median(r['samples_ns'])/1e6 for r in rs]
  gc=', '.join(sorted(set(str(r['after']['MinorCollections']-r['before']['MinorCollections'])+'/'+str(r['after']['FullCollections']-r['before']['FullCollections'])for r in rs)))
  lines.append(f'| {c} | {v} | {statistics.median(ts):.3f} | '+', '.join(f'{t:.3f}'for t in ts)+f' | {gc} | {statistics.median(r["go_after"]["HeapAlloc"]for r in rs)/1048576:.2f} | {statistics.median(r["proc_VmHWM_kib"]for r in rs)/1024:.2f} |')
lines+=['','## Interpretation','','Compact is slower on every workload: every compact process median exceeds every direct16 process median. Smaller struct geometry reduces collection counts, but does not compensate for current helper/adapter costs. Descriptor/layout overhead is a plausible explanation, not established by this unprofiled comparison. This does not predict future compact native-code performance or meet any V8 target. The helper-only runtimes are deliberately not compared against previous optimized native pipelines.','','This is a complete backend implementation comparison, NOT isolated header-size attribution: compact necessarily retires through its start map after forwarding overwrites type metadata, whereas direct16 uses header traversal. Both use exact roots, but layout/traversal/allocation behavior differs. No default adoption is supported by these timings.','','## Independent physical geometry','','Equivalent substrate descriptors at the same configured capacities report identical fixed backing: **28,463,151 bytes** each. This excludes type descriptors, adapter state and Go overhead. Physical object geometry:','','| Shape | Direct extent / stride | Compact payload offset / extent / stride |','|---|---|---|','| i32 struct | 24 / 32 | 4 / 8 / 16 |','| i32[16] array | 80 / 80 | 8 / 72 / 80 |','| i32 + two-reference tree node | 32 / 32 | 4 / 16 / 16 |','','Reduced header bytes do not necessarily reduce stride: the array remains 80 bytes. Fixed preallocated arena/tracing backing does not shrink automatically with smaller objects. Runtime Go heaps remain nearly equal. Lower tree RSS reflects resident pages/collection history, not a reduced configured backing budget. Geometry was measured separately using immutable equivalent descriptors, not unsafe adapter reflection.','','## Separate Compile+Close footprint','','| Case | Backend | Median us/op | Native bytes | Go B/op | Allocs/op |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
g={}
for r in json.loads((p/'compile.json').read_text())['rows']:
 for l in r['stdout'].splitlines():
  m=re.match(r'BenchmarkGCDirectCompileProbe/(\S+)\s+256\s+(\d+) ns/op\s+(\d+) code-B\s+(\d+) B/op\s+(\d+) allocs/op',l)
  if m:g.setdefault((m[1],r['variant']),[]).append(list(map(int,m.groups()[1:])))
for c in dict.fromkeys(r['case']for r in d['rows']):
 for v in ['direct16','compact']:
  t,code,b,a=[statistics.median(x)for x in zip(*g[c,v])];lines.append(f'| {c} | {v} | {t/1000:.3f} | {code} | {b} | {a} |')
lines+=['','Compile measurements are separate from execution and use 256 Compile+Close iterations per case, three rotating processes. They are not peak compiler-memory measurements. All raw output, binary hashes, configurations and counters are retained. Profiling/builds by other workers were excluded during timing; shared-host frequency/scheduling remain uncontrolled. Direct copied/promoted/scan counters are uninstrumented.','']
(p/'summary.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
